refactor: drop the in-repo launcher scripts, document the manual path

The desktop launcher now owns start/stop, so the four .bat files in the repository
were a second copy of the same logic. They are removed, and the README documents the
commands they used to wrap.

- Delete start-potato.bat, stop-potato.bat, autostart-on.bat and autostart-off.bat.
  The desktop entry point no longer references them (it delegates only to
  run_server.py, which stays), so nothing is broken by their removal.
- README: replace the double-click instructions with the actual commands they ran —
  venv, `pip install -e .`, `playwright install chromium`, then run_server.py. The
  background form is documented too, since that is what pythonw is for:
      start "" .venv\Scripts\pythonw run_server.py 18080
  Note there is no longer a script that picks a free port automatically, so the docs
  now say to pass a different port when one is taken.
- CONTRIBUTING: point at run_server.py instead of the deleted script.
- Document in the README that `pip install -e .` installs only what a local install
  needs, and that the closed-by-default integrations live in extras.

Verified after deleting the scripts: the desktop launcher still starts the service
(listening, GET / 200, PID recorded) and stops it, 84 tests pass, ruff clean.
